## Verified facts that are not quality measurements

From OpenCode's usage data (page updated 2026-10-02T15:40Z). These measure adoption, not
capability — logged so a future revision does not mistake them for scores:

- **255B tokens** over the past two months, **rank #18** by tokens across OpenCode last week
  (+100% versus the prior two months); a second, broader ranking page shows it at #9 with 50B
- **55K unique users**; **571,956 completed sessions**; ~445K average tokens per session
- 69.3% of input tokens served from cache; $0.0000 average cost per session; $0 total spend

A caveat on the usage itself: sessions averaging 445K tokens on a route with no published
context window mean the served limit is unstated, and a high cache-hit ratio (69.3%) is a
property of the harness, not the model.

## Normalized scores (1–100)

Not scored. Self-excluded: not one specification and not one benchmark is public. Any Overall
here would be built from the platform's own explicitly-labelled neutral placeholders.

